    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d80">

                <pb facs="0429" n="399" xml:id="pg399"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">S/S–NSC files, lot 66 D 148, “Solarium”</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum to the National Security Council by the
                        Executive Secretary (Lay)</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d80-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1953-07-22">July 22, 1953</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <list rendition="#flush" subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <item>Subject:</item>
                    <item>Project Solarium</item>
                </list>
                <list rendition="#flush" type="references">
                    <item>Reference: NSC Action No. 853–c<anchor
                            n="2" xml:id="d80-f2"/></item>
                </list>
                <p>In accordance with NSC Action No. 853–c,
                    summaries of Project Solarium presentations and written reports, prepared by the
                        NSC staff and concurred in by Solarium Task
                    Force representatives, are submitted herewith as a basis for discussion by the
                    Council at its meeting on July 30, together with a summary of the principal
                    points made during discussion following the presentation to the National
                    Security Council on July 16, 1953.</p>
                <p>As background, there follows a brief summary of the instructions to the Task
                    Forces defining the three alternative policies which they were asked to
                    develop:</p>
                <p>[Here follow summary instructions which appear at the beginning of the summaries
                    of the Task Force presentations included in the enclosure.]</p>



                <xi:include href="d80-a1.xml" xpointer="d80-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d80-a2.xml" xpointer="d80-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d80-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d80-f1-content">
                <p>Copies to the Secretary of the Treasury, the Attorney General, the Directors of
                    the Bureau of the Budget and Central Intelligence, and the Chairmen of the Joint
                    Chiefs of Staff and the Atomic Energy Commission.</p>
            </note>
